592186120716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120715 #edb/ref 1061 17922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120715 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c247ca81-f4a5-53d1-8429-f69593877343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120715 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120716 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120716 #edb/ref 1061 17923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120716 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7a8bd938-5945-5ebb-a062-1d4409d4ccd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120716 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120717 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120717 #edb/ref 1061 17924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120717 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "38691512-c8ac-58b3-b639-597249a111ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120717 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120718 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120718 #edb/ref 1061 17925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120718 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4e18819d-30d0-5673-a2f4-2264aa09fbde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120718 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120719 #edb/ref 1061 17926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120719 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "311c08f2-aa3d-5ea5-8386-44e9771e47c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120719 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121050 #edb/ref 1064 "If we are given an equation of a plane using the dot product, we can always obtain an equation in terms of $x,$ $y,$ and $z.$ For example, suppose we have the plane that passes through the point $P(-7,5,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 3,-6,5 \\rangle.$\n\nFirst, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -7,5,-2 \\rangle,$ and we can write down the equation of the plane using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ & =⟨-7,5,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ & =-61\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation, we substitute $\\mathbf{r}=\\langle x,y,z \\rangle$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ & =-61 \\\\ 3x-6y+5z & =-61 \\\\ 3x-6y+5z+61 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis final equation is called the **Cartesian equation of the plane**.\n\n![](images/77/77f18981dda500889655225eabbec730b7b295e6b16cec1700d56c2e27e0ac91.png)\n\nNote that in the equation \n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}3}x+({\\color{blue}-6})y+{\\color{blue}5}z+61 = 0,\n$$\n\nthe coefficients next to $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ are the coordinates of the normal vector \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\langle {\\color{blue}3},{\\color{blue}-6},{\\color{blue}5} \\rangle\n$$\n\n." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121050 #edb/ref 1065 3256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121050 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "81332607-6152-5770-b33d-8b80c630fc8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121050 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260021 #edb/ref 1080 "(r-⟨0,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,4,-4⟩=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260021 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260021 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0f87268c-9742-5090-b7cb-521a5d8bbe66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261300 #edb/ref 1080 "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨-4,4,-2⟩=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261300 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261300 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a390ff13-0937-5eb3-b38b-3df5883b8889" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261844 #edb/ref 1080 "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,-2,4⟩=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261844 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261844 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "def43d7d-583f-5acb-a4e0-a37562571a5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262013 #edb/ref 1080 "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262013 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262013 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f4c13bd5-c05b-5f70-93b5-0ba177da222f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262119 #edb/ref 1080 "(r-⟨0,0,2⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,2⟩=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262119 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262119 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ffcc7a65-376c-57d0-ac3e-a501019e18ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186262013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186262119 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262329 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262329 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262329 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186262013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262329 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7b80e560-2ad7-58b7-9b2c-28eb67acbc7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262889 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262889 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128380" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262889 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262889 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the Cartesian equation $4x+4y-2z=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262889 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f6aca53-4308-58bc-afcc-f2738d69d1e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262889 #edb/ref 1074 "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨4,4,-2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+4y-2z & =0 \\\\ 2z & =4x+4y \\\\ z & =2x+2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=0.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308836 #edb/ref 1080 "-5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308836 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308836 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ccc2dae-6d3d-5c97-a2ff-2660720cb731" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309261 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309261 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309261 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "43ac71e4-1f43-51f8-bfa4-a92855f4700b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309413 #edb/ref 1080 "12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309413 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309413 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "580b7964-a0b4-59ea-bd21-b56d80484ba8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311144 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186309261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311144 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311144 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311144 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186309261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311144 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7faaceec-cd8b-568a-858c-271760090279" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311213 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186309413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311213 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311213 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311213 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186309413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311213 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "93f3390e-533a-5d25-83c0-c5daa77f3ccf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311226 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186308836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311226 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311226 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311226 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186308836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311226 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "95d0ab30-64b1-59c5-b1be-e3cbd8256de2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311671 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311671 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311671 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311671 #edb/ref 1069 "q-336241" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311671 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311671 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the Cartesian equation $12y-6z-30=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,0,$\n{{field-1}}\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,$\n{{field-2}}\n,\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩=0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311671 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04886b81-54da-502a-b95c-1502eb418ce2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311671 #edb/ref 1074 "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨0,12,-6⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12y-6z-30 & =0 \\\\ -6z & =-12y+30 \\\\ z & =2y-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $y=0$, we get $z=-5.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-5)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-5⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-5⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,12,-6⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
